  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="846710b4-359b-5db4-86ab-dda581c97eeb" activityNameId="a1c50c13-dbab-5a52-a4b8-03e1b9077f64" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Ferrochromium, high-carbon, 68% Cr, at regional storage</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Ferrochromium, high-carbon, 68% Cr, at regional storage
The module describes the consump-tion of chromite in Europe in 1994. It is designed for the use of chromite as intermediary product in the pro-duction of ferrochromium, dichro-mate and refractories. This module does not consider secondary sources of chromium. Process data is taken mainly from a material flow analysis for the consumption of chromium compounds in Germany. Results are used as a proxy for the European situation. ;
Synonyms: ferro-chrome, ferrochrome, chromeisen; 
UUID: b896d2ec-abc9-3300-9394-10baf6b94365
The module includes the transportation of high-carbon ferrochromium to Europe. No secondary production considered, since secondary chromium is recycled to the foundries and has to be inventoried in the respective module, i. e. when casting the final rawmaterial in the stainless steel production.
Location: This module relates to the consumption in Europe, although the import mix for Germany is chosen. Production relates to a global average.
Technology: Most transport by ship
Time period: undefined
Production volume: n.a. 350'000 t in GER (1994), no info on consumpt. in RER
Sampling: literature 
Extrapolations: see Geography and Technology
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_b896d2ec-abc9-3300-9394-10baf6b94365.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
